pcLDRGMm","tool_input":{"command":"theseus packet new --help","description":"Show help for spawning a packet"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01ECaSR496mwrUnaF4vF3zzQ","tool_input":{"command":"git checkout -- npm-shrinkwrap.json && npm install --lockfile-version=1 2>&1 | tail -5; git diff --stat; git diff npm-shrinkwrap.json","timeout":600000,"description":"Reinstall keeping lockfile v1, show diff"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FB5MqTPKps9dUiFAoc8hT5","tool_input":{"command":"git checkout -- npm-shrinkwrap.json","description":"Restore shrinkwrap to committed state"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SKGMQnMbC1bychRmsc4Bo8","tool_input":{"command":"node node_modules/typescript/bin/tsc --version","description":"Check installed tsc version"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NHdQ5R2geQLoX6zd7ztjaC","tool_input":{"command":"npx tsc --version","description":"Check tsc version via npx"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":46,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've fixed the three problems from the last rejection, all three acceptance commands pass, and the work is committed on `pkt/PKT-0009` as `d7340e8`. The follow-up packet for linting `.ts` files still has to be created by whoever runs the factory: I couldn't create it from this run (details below).\n\n**What changed this run** (on top of the earlier toolchain and `utilsDocService.ts` work):\n1. **Generated file untracked.** I removed `DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js` from git with `git rm --cached`. The build writes it from `utilsDocService.ts`, and git now ignores it. Git records the change as a rename from `.js` to `.ts`.\n2. **Shrinkwrap now produced by npm.** The earlier hand-written `typescript` entry never gave a working compiler. TypeScript 7 runs on a separate native package per platform, and that entry didn't list them. `tsc` failed with \"Unable to resolve @typescript/typescript-linux-x64\", and `npm ci` rejected the file. I ran `npm install` and then `npm install --lockfile-version=1`. The entry now has its integrity hash, its dependency list and all 20 optional platform packages. A clean `npm ci` followed by `tsc` works.\n3. **Interop doc updated.** The old note about the hand-written entry is replaced by a recipe for changing root dependencies, a warning about the platform packages, and a line saying the lint follow-up packet is still pending.\n\n**Checks after a clean `npm ci`:**\n- `npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` passes.\n- `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` passes: 14/14 suites, 554 tests passed and 1 skipped. It rebuilds the `.js` first, and stack traces point at the matching `.ts` line.\n- `npm run lint:check` passes with no errors. Its one warning is in AdminPanel and is not from this packet.\n- The packet is within budget: 11 files and 531 changed lines since the claim (limits are 14 and 1,500).\n\n**Decisions:**\n- **Shrinkwrap format:** I kept the shrinkwrap at lockfile v1, as every package in this repo uses. A plain `npm install` would have converted it to v3, about 9,000 changed lines and far over the budget.\n- **Earlier decisions unchanged:** `.js` is written next to the `.ts` and not committed, `tsc` only type-checks, Node's built-in type stripping does the build, and Jest runs the freshly rebuilt `.js`.\n\n**Not done:**\n- **Lint follow-up packet:** creating it means running `theseus packet new` and writing under `.theseus/queue/`. This run forbade queue writes and the command needed an approval I didn't have. The reviewer asked for it last time, so they may raise it again. It is recorded in the interop doc.\n- **Friction log:** I didn't append to `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` because it is outside the packet's target. The friction worth recording is that the run rules and the method's \"spawn a packet\" rule contradict each other.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas** (now in the interop doc):\n- In TypeScript 7, `node_modules/typescript` is only a launcher. `tsc` works only when the platform package is installed, so test with `npm ci` and then `tsc`, not just by checking that the package exists.\n- To keep a v1 shrinkwrap: run `npm install` first (it writes v3 and resolves everything), then `npm install --lockfile-version=1`. Converting straight from the old v1 file silently drops the optional platform packages.\n- After ignoring a generated `.js`, check that `git ls-files <file>` prints nothing. If it still lists the file, git keeps tracking it despite `.gitignore`.","ttft_ms":1538,"type":"result","duration_ms":177302,"uuid":"637c60a3-4b9c-4669-93d6-e8a884588f00","ttft_stream_ms":1109,"time_to_request_ms":583,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":391,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":31,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":10,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":2,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":15,"query_setup":5,"auto_mode_context_wait":18,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":36,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":3,"request_build":12},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":96,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":324,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":244,"process_anon_mib_result":149,"process_peak_rss_mib":268,"process_cpu_ms_turn":5449,"process_wall_ms_turn":177301,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":2257,"process_wall_ms_streaming":113570,"main_stream_count"